---
import Page from "@layouts/Page.astro";
import Section from "@components/Section.astro";
import SectionHead from "@components/SectionHead.astro";
import SectionSub from "@components/SectionSub.astro";
import SectionSub2Col from "@components/SectionSub2Col.astro";
import Details from "@components/Details.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

const title = "Redi-Rock Structures of O.K.I.";
import BrandGuidelines from "@images/projects/rrs/BrandGuidelines.png";
import BrandGuidelinesPDF from "@assets/Brand Guidelines.pdf";
import Development from "@images/projects/rrs/Development.jpg";
import Documentation from "@images/projects/rrs/Documentation.jpg";
import HomeDesigns from "@images/projects/rrs/HomeDesigns.jpg";
import Logos from "@images/projects/rrs/Logos.png";
import Photography from "@images/projects/rrs/Photography.png";
import Print2024 from "@images/projects/rrs/Print2024.png";
import Prototype from "@images/projects/rrs/Prototype.png";
import SiteOutline from "@images/projects/rrs/SiteOutline.png";
import Template from "@images/projects/rrs/Template.png";
import Workshop from "@images/projects/rrs/RRS Workshop.jpg";

import HomeOld from "@images/projects/rrs/home-old.jpg";
import HomeNew from "@images/projects/rrs/home-new.jpg";

import Calendar2023_01 from "@images/projects/rrs/Calendar2023-01.jpg";
import Calendar2023_02 from "@images/projects/rrs/Calendar2023-02.jpg";
import Calendar2023_03 from "@images/projects/rrs/Calendar2023-03.png";
import Calendar2024_01 from "@images/projects/rrs/Calendar2024-01.jpg";
import Calendar2024_02 from "@images/projects/rrs/Calendar2024-02.jpg";
import Calendar2024_03 from "@images/projects/rrs/Calendar2024-03.jpg";
---

<Page title={title}>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Summary" />
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 typography">
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>Redi-Rock Structures of O.K.I. was in need of a website refresh, both visually and structurally. Teaming up with <a href="https://gretchensteward.crevado.com/" target="_blank">Gretchen Steward of intellifi UX</a>, we defined and updated the client's branding, improved the organization and consistency of the content, and made the interface look cleaner and more modern.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Roles and Timeline" />
    <SectionSub>
      <Details>
        <h3 slot="summaryTitle" class="mb-0">Branding</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
          <SectionSub2Col>
            <h4 slot="title">Workshop</h4>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
              <p>We conducted a branding workshop with the owners and sales directors to help define the company brand and direct design and copywriting.</p>
              <Image src={Workshop} alt="large post-it notes" />
            </div>
          </SectionSub2Col>
          <SectionSub2Col>
            <h4 slot="title">Logo</h4>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
              <p>Using the branding workshop findings as guidance, I explored new logos and color palettes. We ultimately arrived at a refined version of the existing logo with new brand colors and variations.</p>
              <Image src={Logos} alt="logos" />
            </div>
          </SectionSub2Col>
          <SectionSub2Col>
            <h4 slot="title">Guidelines</h4>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
              <p>Next, we designed and authored <a href={BrandGuidelinesPDF} target="_blank">branding guidelines</a> to codify logo usage, typography, colors, written voice, and photography rules.</p>
              <Image src={BrandGuidelines} alt="" />
            </div>
          </SectionSub2Col>
          <SectionSub2Col>
            <h4 slot="title">Print</h4>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
              <p>Before we tackled the website, I updated the client’s print collateral with the refreshed logo, colors, and typography.</p>
              <Image src={Print2024} alt="Examples of print pieces with updated branding." />
            </div>
          </SectionSub2Col>
          <SectionSub2Col>
            <h4 slot="title">Photography</h4>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
              <p>Following the new branding guidelines, we directed a photography session that captured the production facilities, products, examples of product use, and various team members.</p>
              <Image src={Photography} alt="" />
            </div>
          </SectionSub2Col>
        </div>
      </Details>
      <Details>
        <h3 slot="summaryTitle" class="mb-0">Information Architecture and Content Strategy</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
          <SectionSub2Col>
            <h4 slot="title">Site Structure</h4>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
              <p>Drawing from the structure of the Redi-Rock International site, as well as the site visitors identified in the branding workshop, we organized the content to better showcase the products, their environmental uses, and existing projects they were used in.</p>
              <Image src={SiteOutline} alt="" />
            </div>
          </SectionSub2Col>
          <SectionSub2Col>
            <h4 slot="title">Page Structure</h4>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
              <p>We organized each page template to highlight the most important information the target visitors would be seeking. Additional information related to each product, industry, and project case study was included in the page templates to provide relevant, cross-linked content.</p>
              <Image src={Template} alt="" />
            </div>
          </SectionSub2Col>
        </div>
      </Details>
      <Details>
        <h3 slot="summaryTitle" class="mb-0">Protyping</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <p>Using Figma, I connected the individual wireframe pages together to validate the organization and navigation. It was important at this stage to have the client test drive the prototype and sign off on the organization and layouts before proceeding with the UI design.</p>
          <Image src={Prototype} alt="" />
        </div>
      </Details>
      <Details>
        <h3 slot="summaryTitle" class="mb-0">UI Design</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <p>Continuing in Figma, we presented several design options that struck a good balance of delivering product and company information while keeping the consistent visual and written voice established in the branding guidelines. Once the client approved one of the themes, I applied the design to the interior templates and components.</p>
          <Image src={HomeDesigns} alt="" />
        </div>
      </Details>
      <Details>
        <h3 slot="summaryTitle" class="mb-0">Development</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <div>
            <p>Using the reusable templates and components in Figma laid the groundwork for creating these reusable items in WordPress. Using Oxygen Builder for WordPress, I created a global toolkit of colors, fonts, templates, and reusable components. Not only did this creation of global elements allow for future scaling of the website, it also allowed for rapid creation and content population of the pages from Figma to WordPress.</p>
            <p>I also created custom tools within the WordPress admin to allow the client to easily add team members, entries to the company timeline, and automatic placement of new products and project case studies based on a predefined metatag structure.</p>
          </div>
          <Image src={Development} alt="" />
        </div>
      </Details>
      <Details>
        <h3 slot="summaryTitle" class="mb-0">Documentation and Training</h3>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
          <p>I created technical documentation, within the WordPress admin, which contained instructions on how to create and update key pieces of information in the site. Being able to keep this type of documentation within the site is a nice upgrade from my previous practices of authoring and delivering in a separate environment (e.g. Google Docs) from the functioning site.</p>
          <Image src={Documentation} alt="" />
        </div>
      </Details>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Results" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap gap-16">
        <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap">
          <h3>Home Page</h3>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 grid-rows-1 gap-4">
            <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap">
              <h4>Before</h4>
              <Image src={HomeOld} alt="View of the home page before my work." class="outline outline-indigo-100" />
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap">
              <h4>After</h4>
              <Image src={HomeNew} alt="View of the home page after my work." class="outline outline-indigo-100" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap">
          <h3>Calendar</h3>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 grid-rows-1 gap-4">
            <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap">
              <h4>Before</h4>
              <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap gap-4">
                <Image src={Calendar2023_01} alt="2023 Calendar Cover" class="outline outline-indigo-100" />
                <Image src={Calendar2023_02} alt="2023 Calendar Month Image" class="outline outline-indigo-100" />
                <Image src={Calendar2023_03} alt="2023 Calendar Month Date Grid" class="outline outline-indigo-100" />
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap">
              <h4>After</h4>
              <div class="flex flex-col flex-nowrap gap-4">
                <Image src={Calendar2024_01} alt="2024 Calendar Cover" class="outline outline-indigo-100" />
                <Image src={Calendar2024_02} alt="2024 Calendar Month Image" class="outline outline-indigo-100" />
                <Image src={Calendar2024_03} alt="2024 Calendar Month Date Grid" class="outline outline-indigo-100" />
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
</Page>
